    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n4345" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄλκῐμος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, also
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">η</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>
		<i><span class="en">
			S.
			<u>Aj.</u>
			401
		</span></i>: (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλκή</span>):—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>stout, brave</i>, of men and
			things, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Τρῶες, ἔγχος, δοῦρε</span>,
				<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				11.483
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				3.338
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				22.125
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἦτορ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Callin.
					1.10
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θυμός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Tyrt.
					10.17
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νέκυς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>Pae.</u>
					6.98
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δράκων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Epich.
					60
				</span></i>
			: 
				Comp.
			
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ώτερος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					1.79
				</span></i>
			,<i><span class="en">
				103
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				607a11
			</span></i>, etc.: 
				Sup.
			
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ώτατος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Ph.</u>
					743
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				6.5.9
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄ. τὰ πολεμικά</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					3.4
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐς ἀλκὴν ἄλκιμα</span> ib.
				<i><span class="en">
				110
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄ. μάχη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Heracl.</u>
					683
				</span></i>
			:—prov., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πάλαι ποτ᾽ ἦσαν
				ἄλκιμοι Μιλήσιοι</span> `times are changed', <i><span class="en">
				Anacr.
				85
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Pl.</u>
				1002
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Philostr.
				<u>VS</u>
				1.22.4
			</span></i>:—less common in Prose, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				614b
			</span></i> (with play on <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀλκίνου</span>),
				<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				628b6
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>fortifying</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕδωρ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.669b
				</span></i>
			 s.v.l.; <i>giving succour,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				PMag.Leid.W.
				14.10
			</span></i>.</div>
